new file mode 100644
index 0000000..35cb9cf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/privacy-audit.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Privacy audit
+
+Scope: sign-in, sign-up, shared page layout, document response headers, and the privacy notice.
+
+| Finding | Change |
+| --- | --- |
+| Global, unversioned analytics could observe credentials and visits. | Removed the analytics loader and the commented advertising loader; removed the shared ad-slot initialization. No consent dialog is needed for scripts that are no longer loaded. |
+| Google Fonts and preconnects disclosed visits automatically. | Removed the stylesheet and connections, and used a system serif font. |
+| Credential submission to an external demo API was undisclosed. | Added a shared notice before both forms and field-specific explanations; retained only username and password. |
+| Raw backend errors could disclose service details or account existence. | Replaced returned error text with generic local messages and stopped parsing unused response bodies. |
+| Form identifiers and autofill hints were missing. | Added names, password-manager autocomplete, required-field labels, and accessible help text. Set method to POST so a missing client handler cannot put credentials into a URL; submit remains disabled until hydration, with a no-JavaScript notice. |
+| Credentials could linger after submission. | Clear passwords after success, service failure, or network failure; clear usernames on success. No token or credential persistence was added. Browser password-manager storage remains user-controlled. |
+| Requests inherited browser defaults. | Explicitly omit cookies and referrers, request no caching, and reject redirects on credential fetches. This cannot control the external server's logging or retention. |
+| Document privacy policies were absent. | Add no-referrer and a restrictive Permissions-Policy in middleware for HTML responses, including error pages. Add an early referrer meta fallback. Mark account documents no-store and add nosniff to HTML responses. |
+| Privacy policy was generic and incomplete. | Describe actual data flows and the known limits of the demo. |
+
+## Remaining boundaries
+
+The external authentication backend is not in this repository. Its password hashing, retention, deletion, access controls, and request logging still need a service-owner review before collecting real user data. The existing login only reports success; this change does not invent session management or account controls.
+
+Article-specific teaching examples (including cookies) and externally hosted article images remain. Server-side reading-list sessions remain. The policy discloses these rather than claiming the entire site is cookie-free or third-party-free. Hosting/CDN logs are outside the repository's control.
+
+A full script CSP/Trusted Types rollout needs a separate compatibility audit of Astro hydration, client routing, and article demonstration scripts. Do not add an untested blanket script policy or a report collector that could itself collect personal data.
+
+## Verification
+
+Completed checks:
+
+- `pnpm run build` passed. Existing Vite plugin deprecation and dynamic-route `getStaticPaths` warnings remain.
+- Isolated middleware checks passed for document headers, account no-store policy with and without trailing slashes, reading-list initialization, and unchanged API headers.
+- Mocked form-handler checks passed for both forms on success, service failure, and network failure: only the two credential fields were sent, privacy request flags were present, passwords were cleared, and raw service details were not exposed.
+- `git diff --check` passed; source checks confirmed the shared layout has no analytics, ad loader, or Google Fonts references.
+
+No browser verification, server startup, server-entrypoint imports, or live authentication API requests were performed.
+
+Header references: [Referrer-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Referrer-Policy) and [Permissions-Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Permissions-Policy).
