-    <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
-    <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <h2>This is a demonstration site</h2>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is a demo for Chrome DevTools. You can read it without creating an account. Use made-up credentials for account features, and never submit a real name, email address, or a password you use elsewhere.</p>
+
+    <h2>What the account forms send and why</h2>
+    <p>Sign-up sends only a username and password to create a demo account. Sign-in sends the same two fields to check those credentials. Both forms send an HTTPS POST request directly from your browser to the external service at <code class="break-all">https://us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/api/</code>, using the <code>register</code> or <code>login</code> endpoint. That service also receives network information such as your IP address and browser request headers.</p>
+    <p>The forms omit cookies from these requests, suppress the referring page URL, and request no caching. They do not save credentials or returned tokens in browser storage or log them to the console. The password field is cleared after each submission attempt; the username is cleared after a successful response. Your browser or password manager may offer to save credentials according to your own settings.</p>
+
+    <h2>Retention and account controls</h2>
+    <p>The external authentication service is outside this application's codebase. Its server-side storage, logging, password protection, and retention period have not been verified here. This demo does not provide account export, correction, or deletion controls. Do not submit personal data on the assumption that it can be deleted through this site.</p>
+
+    <h2>Third-party resources and browser storage</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout loads no third-party analytics, advertising scripts, or remote fonts. Account forms are not instrumented for analytics. Some articles contain externally hosted images; loading them discloses network information to the image host. Page requests use a no-referrer policy to avoid sending the referring page URL.</p>
+    <p>Reading-list features use server-side session storage and may require a session cookie. Some article demonstrations also use cookies for their example API requests. These are separate from the account forms; the forms do not create a persistent sign-in session. Infrastructure serving this site and external resources may keep request logs; their retention is not configured by this application.</p>
+
+    <h2>Browser permissions</h2>
+    <p>Document responses disable camera, microphone, location, motion sensors, payment, and USB access through a Permissions-Policy header. The account forms do not request device permissions or add marketing fields.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
